s follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 12 & 24 & 12\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=1-2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n5a+\\frac{b}{c}=5\\cdot 1+\\frac{(-2)}{1}=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186367453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367451 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c701115a-b609-5cd4-a698-790dbbe0d2a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367452 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367452 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367452 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0366dc6-1996-570e-840e-8c80856c8afa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367453 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367453 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367453 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b06eb22-5e54-52d9-a5d8-de25d113e619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367454 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367454